<AddOnInstructionDefinitions Use="Context">
<EncodedData EncodedType="AddOnInstructionDefinition" Name="Dvc_2198ABQE_1CH" Revision="2.0" RevisionExtension=".01" Vendor="Rockwell Automation" EditedDate="2016-11-29T08:59:16.544Z" SoftwareRevision="v30.00" EncryptionConfig="9">
<Description>
<![CDATA[2198-ABQE - Single Channel Encoder Output]]>
</Description>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[Release]]>
</RevisionNote>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[============================================================
Instruction Overview:
-----
Dvc_2198ABQE_1CH AOI is a 1 axis channel interface between the controller position information and the encoder emulator output pulses. Normally it should be called in the Motion Group Execution event task, which runs at the base Coarse Update Period (CUP) rate. Also the AOI instruction can only be called with the always TRUE enable in.

The Cycle Start Time attribute in the motion group object representing the start time of each CUP and the Planner Command Position Integer and the Planner Command Position Fractional attributes in the motion axis object representing precise command position information will be copied to the IO connection output assembly of the controlled emulator module with each axis CUP rate. The Update ID will be incremented by 1 after each copy so that the encoder emulator will know whether the received data is refreshed or not. 

Besides the Controller Timestamp and PositionInt and Fractional fields of the IO connection output assembly, the base Update Period, channel Coarse Update Period, Controller Time Offset and the Grand Master ID are also updated in the AOI instruction with the rate of base CUP. 


Instruction Execution:
-----
Instruction - Level
Command Inputs - Edge

Supplemental Descriptions:
-----

Module-defined Data Type: AB:2198_ABQE:I:0

RunMode 
Indicates the module’s operating state. 0 = Idle, 1 = Run mode

ConnectionFaulted
Indicates if a connection is running. 0 = Connection running, 1 = Connection not running

DiagnosticActive
Indicates if any diagnostics are active or if the prognostics threshold is reached.  0 = No diagnostics are active, 1 = One or more diagnostics are active or the prognostics threshold is reached.

CIPSyncValid
Indicates whether the module is synced with a 1588 master. 0 = The module is not synchronized and cannot provide a valid output, 1 = The module is synchronized and can provide a valid output

CIPSyncTimeout
Indicates that the module was once synced with a 1588 master, but is no longer synchronized due to a timeout.  0 = A valid time master has not timed out, 1 = A valid time master was detected, but the time master has timed out.

DiagnosticSequenceCount 
A counter that increments each time a distinct diagnostic condition is detected, and when a distinct diagnostic condition transitions from detected to not detected. Set to zero by product reset or power cycle.  Wraps from 255 (-1) to 1 skipping zero. | -128…127  The value of 0 is skipped except during module power-up.

RuntimeErrorFault
The module has an internal software error. Communication may be unreliable.  0 = Fault is not active, 1 = Fault is active.

ClockSkewFault
The local clock has been skewed with the grandmaster clock for a time exceeding the fault threshold.  0 = Fault is not active, 1 = Fault is active.

ClockSyncFault
The local clock has lost synchronization with the grandmaster clock for a time exceeding the fault threshold.  0 = Fault is not active, 1 = Fault is active.

ClockSyncAlarm	
The local clock has lost synchronization with the grandmaster clock for a time exceeding the alarm threshold.  0 = Alarm is not active, 1 = Alarm is active.

ClockJitterAlarm
Jitter between the local clock and grandmaster clock has occurred for a time exceeding the alarm threshold.  0 = Alarm is not active, 1 = Alarm is active

ClockSkewAlarm
The local clock has been skewed with the grandmaster clock for a time exceeding the alarm threshold.  0 = Alarm is not active, 1 = Alarm is active

IPAddressMismatch
The IP address switch values have been changed after the module has detected the switch values and used them to set the IP address.  0 = Alarm is not active, 1 = Alarm is active

SyncStatus
The module synchronization status.  0 = Synchronized, 1 = Not Synchronized, 2 = Incorrect Grandmaster Clock,  3 = Clock Skewed, 4 = Initializing, 


Module-defined Data Type: AB:2198_Channel:I:0

FrequencyFault
The channel has limited the output frequency to the Frequency Limit for a time period exceeding the Frequency Limit Fault Time.  0 = Fault is not active, 1 = Fault is active

Fault
A fault exists that disables the channel output signal.  0 = Fault is not active, 1 = Fault is active

Uncertain
Detects if an alarm exists that may adversely affect the channel output signal or if the Encoder Output 
Emulator has not yet synchronized with the controller.  0 = Uncertain is not active, 1 = Uncertain is active

InternalFault
Detects if the channel has an internal hardware error.  0 = Fault is not active, 1 = Fault is active

FieldPowerOff 
Detects if an external power supply is connected. An external supply is required to support single ended output signals.  0 = An external power supply for single ended outputs is detected, 1 = An external power supply for single ended outputs is not detected.

FieldPowerFault
Detects if the Signal Type and Field Power are compatible. Field power must be disconnected for a Differential Signal Type. Field power must be connected for a Single Ended Signal Type.	0 = Fault is not active, 1 = Fault is active

PositionUpdateFault
Detects if the channel is receiving position updates from the controller at a regular interval.  0 = Fault is not active, 1 = Fault is active

UpdatePeriodFault
Detects if the Axis update period being emulated on this channel is outside of the capability of the module.  0 = Fault is not active, 1 = Fault is active

FrequencyAlarm
Detects if the channel is limiting the output frequency to the Frequency Limit.  0 = Alarm is not active, 1 = Alarm is active

RPIUpdatePeriodMismatch
Detects when the RPI of the module connection is slower than the Axis update period being emulated on this channel.  0 = Mismatch is not active, 1 = Mismatch is active

UpdateID
A counter heartbeat to confirm the AOI is receiving updates from the channel.  Min SINT...Max SINT
State

Operational State of the channel.  0 = Initializing, 1 = Standby, 2 = Stopped, 3 = Running, 4 = Major Faulted, 5 = Minor Faulted

PositionTrackingStatus
Indicates if the channel output signal is tracking the position input. This is always true for the incremental Startup Method.  It is true for Absolute Startup Method once the output signal has caught up to the input position.  0 = Output is not tracking the input position, 1 = Output is tracking the input position

RelativePosition	
Indicates the current position of the channel within the channel Resolution.  0 ...(Resolution -1)


Module-defined Data Type: AB:2198_ABQE:O:0

LocalClockOffset[X]
Identifies the amount of clock skew that is allowed between the local clock time and the grandmaster clock time.  Min DINT...Max DINT

GrandMasterClockID[X]
Identifier of the location of the grandmaster clock on the network.  Min SINT...Max SINT


Module-defined Data Type: AB:2198_Channel:O:0

OutputEn
Enables or disables the channel output pulses.	0 = Output signals are disabled, 1 = Output signals are enabled


Sts_ERR Enumeration:
Value	Error Description

0	No errors present.	
1010	Time synchronization is disabled.  Enable controller time synchronization.
1011	Time synchronization lost. If the controller is a time slave, time sync has been lost for more than 60 seconds.
1012	Motion Event Task overrun happened.
1013	Connected Encoder Emulator in faulty state.
1014	Invalid Position Mode configuration in the virtual axis configured to the 1st channel.  Axis must be configured as linear.
1015	Invalid Position Mode Configuration in the virtual axis configured to the 2nd channel.  Axis must be configured as linear.


Sts_EXERR Enumeration:
If an instruction error occurs internally, the value of the instruction*.ERR DINT will be placed in Sts_EXERR.


Revision Notes:
-----
Type Codes
CI	-Continuous Improvement
AC	-Anomaly Correction

2.0.00 – Release
2.0.01 – Always TRUE enable in added in AOI Help.


